{"type": "restate", "vol": "V09", "n": 6, "severity": "minor", "items": ["V09-0620", "V09-0621", "V09-0629", "V09-0633", "V09-0634", "V10-0186"], "where": "V09 §4.20 'Constants of this section' table and §4.20.1 (3)-(4)", "claim": "Rule R-c of file f (volume 11 owns values) is not followed: the table restates V11 cells with their numbers (terrace.stepMinCm 60 cm, terrace.slopeMin 0.15, aqueduct.sourceReachKm 10 km, aqueduct.gradient [0.0003, 0.003]) and gives terrace.retainingReachM 15 m, flatDepthM 12 m, coverShare 0.8 two homes ('our own … a cell of volume 11's terrace table'); §4.20.1 (4) restates V10's encoders.terrace.radiusM default (25 m). Constants read by the engine's dry run (the step sampling 2 m / ± 3 m, the effects cap 50) are homed in the application volume though the dry run is the base's (§7.1, BCR-V9-27). The deck landmark row already shows the right form ('volume 11's cell, cited, not a constant of this volume'). The value is circular: V10 §2.10 content.encoders gives terrace radius 25 m \"calibrate-later against V09's terrace brush default\" while V09 §4.20.1 (4) gives the default as \"volume 10's encoders.terrace.radiusM\".", "hint": "Cite V11's cells by name without numbers; move dry-run constants (sampling, effects cap) to their engine home (the base's item-110 section / BCR-V9-27's PreviewResult text) or V11's table; keep in V09 only shell constants (closing radius, preview-on-release km if the shell reads it, tierStep snap)."}
