{"type": "iconf", "vol": "V09", "n": 4, "severity": "minor", "items": ["V09-0566", "V09-0686"], "where": "V09 §4.15 'Never colour alone' vs §5.4 'Supply links'", "claim": "§4.15 says the link view 'draws each goods family with its own dash pattern (five patterns) besides its colour', while §5.4 draws links 'coloured by the good's family … dashed where the satisfaction is below 1' and impaired chains 'with a gap every 20 px'. Dashing carries three different meanings (goods family, low satisfaction, impaired chain), so a dashed link is ambiguous and the second cue for colour is undefined.", "hint": "Give each cue one channel: e.g. goods family = colour + dash pattern (five), satisfaction < 1 = reduced opacity or a hollow arrowhead, impaired chain = half width with gaps; state it once in §5.4 and cite from §4.15 (this also serves item 112 (a)'s second cue)."}
