{"type": "gmiss", "vol": "V09", "n": 2, "severity": "major", "items": ["V09-0684", "V09-0701"], "where": "V09 §5.4 Show menu, §5.12 Settings, §7 tests vs g item 112", "claim": "Item 112 names V09 for 'the view settings, the trial's running': (a) every style and thematic view that encodes meaning in colour gets a second cue and a checked variant for the three common colour deficiencies, selectable in the view settings; (b) a game-master trial (ten to twenty SettlementForge game masters, at least two sessions of play, before public release; thanks by credit and early access, no payments). V09 has no deficiency-variant selector in Settings or the Show menu / Dress panel, no second-cue rule for its own thematic views (Wealth, Quarters, Who knows, Coverage, Voids, Shade), and no trial protocol beside the first-five-minutes rounds (grep 'colour-blind', 'deficien', 'trial' of release: 0 hits).", "hint": "Add the view setting (a Dress/Settings chip: 'Colour vision: usual · red-weak · green-weak · blue-weak', a view key), the second cue per V09 thematic view, and a §7 protocol section for the pre-release GM trial (recruitment from SettlementForge's community, sessions, record to V12, release-gate bar); cite item 112 and J122."}
