{"type": "xagree", "vol": "V09", "n": 1, "severity": "major", "items": ["V09-0129", "V09-0130", "V09-0296", "V09-1036", "V09-1037", "V10-0480", "V10-0481"], "where": "V09 §2.6 (screen → row table), §4.7, §10.2 XV-V9-1/XV-V9-2 vs V11 §4.2 (V11 lines 4012-4030)", "claim": "V09 and V11 disagree on the shape of the two document-only tables: (1) V09 writes a kind key 'cls:<class>' (a roster class no dossier record binds); V11 lists three key forms only (uid:, cat:, use:); (2) V09 writes split:false and V11's quarter, place and pin cells under the KIND key ('Keep works and shop together for every {kind}', 'Put them in {quarter}', 'Put them here', 'Keep them where they are'), while V11 gives uid: {profile, familyWeights, quarter} and cat: {profile, familyWeights} and puts place, pin and split on use: rows only; (3) V09 says a use: key 'admits the split cell only', V11's use: row carries place, pin, split and specialisation; (4) V09's link view writes siting.linkEdits {avoid: [provider]} ('Cut this link'), V11 §4.2's cells are {bindTo?, cut?} (only V11's wiring row W42 mentions avoid). XV-V9-1 and XV-V9-2 are not marked Met and are not closed at their destination. V10 §4.1's encoders write the same disputed forms (link avoid list; merge allOfKind with cls:<class>).", "hint": "Rule the tables' shape once at V11 §4.2 (the owner of the tables): add cls: and avoid, and state which cells each key form admits; V09 §2.6 cites it and maps each screen to a cell V11 declares; mark XV-V9-1/2 closed."}
