{"type": "handoff", "vol": "V09", "n": 2, "severity": "minor", "items": ["V09-1039", "V09-1044", "V09-1048", "V09-1049", "V09-1050"], "where": "V09 §10.2 XV-V9-4, XV-V9-9, XV-V9-13, XV-V9-14, XV-V9-15 (status)", "claim": "These requests are met at their destinations (V04 line 3794 under/wayIn; V07 line 4206 showCircuit; V11 lines 688-689 retainingReachM, flatDepthM; V04 line 404 archVault; V03 line 403 basement/crypt/ring) but V9 §10.2 still states them as open requests, so the table no longer tells which hand-offs are closed (principle (10)).", "hint": "Mark them Met with their destination sections (and drop the 'Was:' narration that the Met rows carry)."}
{"type": "xconf", "vol": "V09", "n": 1, "severity": "major", "items": ["V09-1002", "V09-0121"], "where": "V09 §10.1 BCR-V9-3 (applied as written by file f item 277) vs V09 §2.4 WorkingLayer", "claim": "BCR-V9-3's new §2.9 text defines workingLayer as 'the layer the tools act on — ground, a sky island's PlatKey, or an underground depth band', while V9 §2.4 types WorkingLayer as {layer 'ground'} / {layer 'sky'; key} / {layer 'underground'} and says 'the band is the view key depthBand alone (§2.9), never copied here'. Applying item 277 as written would put a band into workingLayer, contradicting the volume's type and V04's depthBand key.", "hint": "Correct BCR-V9-3's text (and file f item 277's application) to 'ground, a sky island's PlatKey, or the underground (its band the view key depthBand)'."}
