{"type": "narr", "vol": "V09", "n": 7, "severity": "minor", "items": ["V09-1071", "V09-1072"], "where": "V09 §12 (lines 4292-4474, about 180 lines)", "claim": "After its two core paragraphs, §12 narrates each review round ('The revision (revise-V9)', 'The second round', 'Reconciliation round 1' … 'round 6', each continuation) with what was read, md5s, landed times and which PLAUSIBLE clauses 'moved to CONFIRMED'; this is how the text evolved (principle (5)), and it restates hand-off statuses that §10.2 carries. The CONFIRMED/PLAUSIBLE facts that remain true fit in the two core paragraphs.", "hint": "Fold the still-PLAUSIBLE constants and budgets into the core PLAUSIBLE paragraph; drop the per-round narration (the validation records keep it)."}
{"type": "xagree", "vol": "V09", "n": 3, "severity": "major", "items": ["V09-0653", "V09-1075", "V10-0782"], "where": "V09 §4.9 catalogue (tier/stack/deck bend rows) and §4.20.5 vs V02 §1b bend ids (V02 line 303, 2695)", "claim": "V02 names its stacked-massing and deck bends bend.tiers.stepped, .none, .axial, .internal, .count, .step, bend.stack.groundWing, .roof, .base, bend.deck.single, bend.deck.basement, bend.building.remove, bend.wing.grow, bend.family.nearest, bend.room.passage, bend.row.plotLine, and states 'volume 9's (X21) … under the ids of V2 §1b'. V09's catalogue holds bend.tiers.count and bend.tiers.step (shared) but otherwise bend.tiers.flights, bend.tier.height, bend.stack.internalSolid, .removeStair, .addWing, .deck, .notStepped and bend.deck.floors — none of which V02 emits — and has no row for fourteen of V02's ids. IN-V09-4 ('every bend of V2 §1b … has a catalogue row') was never applied to §4.9. The engine would emit keys with no row (T-V9-15 fails CI) and V09's rows would have no producer. V10's IN-V10-3 has the clerk \"word each bend of V2 §1b\", which it can only do through V09's rows.", "hint": "Take V2 §1b's bend ids as the one set (V02 owns the dry run): write one §4.9 row per V02 id with its words and buttons, retire V09's unmatched keys (or V02 adopts them by a ruling), and re-point T-V9-59 and §4.20.5."}
