{"type": "j121", "vol": "V10", "n": 1, "severity": "major", "items": ["V10-0006", "V10-0050", "V10-0170", "V10-0399"], "where": "V10 §0 'Turning it on, and what it costs' (lines 177-183) and §1.3 (\"Other providers or a local model — declined by the brief: the built-in clerk runs on Claude\"); §2.10 default row ops.model.id (claude-opus-5; \"Claude Opus 5.5 is the owner's option (section 11 Q3)\"); §3.16 key row (\"Your Anthropic account has no credit left.\")", "claim": "The plain words fix the provider and key path ('runs on Claude, Anthropic's model … you paste your own Anthropic API key … or the program that embeds the map … provides the connection, or uses its own assistant instead'); J121/J122 decided V10 Q1 (key or relay: follows SettlementForge's AI setup), Q2 (SettlementForge's assistant, driving our tool API) and Q3 (model tier follows SettlementForge; evaluate a cheaper tier before any switch). The SettlementForge module's case is SettlementForge's assistant through the host seam, not the built-in clerk with the user's key.", "hint": "Reword: in the SettlementForge module the assistant, its AI setup and model tier are SettlementForge's (J121/J122) and drive the map's tool API through the host seam; the built-in clerk with a user's key is the standalone case; cite J121/J122."}
