{"type": "xagree", "vol": "V10", "n": 3, "severity": "minor", "items": ["V10-0241", "V10-0242", "V10-0247", "V09-0282"], "where": "V10 §3.3 default lexicon (population rows) vs V09 §4.5 T1 size chips (J-V9.56)", "claim": "The same size words map to different populations on the two surfaces: the clerk's lexicon fixes 'small town' 2 500, 'town' 5 000, 'large town' 8 000, 'small city' 12 000, 'city' 20 000, 'large city' 28 000, 'metropolis' 50 000, while V09's seven size chips with the same words read population quantiles of the rungs' bands from the rung table (TOWN band's 25th, 50th, 85th percentiles; CITY's; METROPOLIS's median). 'A town' asked in words and picked as a chip can give different recipes; one concept has two mappings (principle (2) and (10)).", "hint": "One rule for the size words (the chips' quantile rule read from the rung table) serving the chips and the lexicon; the lexicon rows name the quantile, not a number."}
