{"type": "xagree", "vol": "V10", "n": 4, "severity": "major", "items": ["V10-0355", "V09-0590"], "where": "V10 §3.9a crypt row 'no crypt' vs V09 §4.17.5 crypt line vs V03 (lines 140, J-V3.44)", "claim": "Three texts disagree on a church on wet ground: V10's crypt section words it 'no crypt: ledger slabs in the chancel floor'; V09 §4.17.5 says 'V03's wet-ground fold reads \"floor vaults (wet ground)\"' as a crypt form on the church's Below line; V03 has no floor-vault crypt (J-V3.44: 'flush ledger slabs … in a church without a crypt over a floor-vault \"crypt\"') and lifts an always-crypt on wet ground to a raised-choir crypt (line 140). The panel and the clerk would say different things for one row, and V09's wording names a form V03 rejected.", "hint": "Rule at V03 §3.7.4 (the crypt's owner): wet ground gives a raised-choir crypt for an always class and no crypt with ledger slabs otherwise; V10 §3.9a words both; V09 §4.17.5 cites the rows (dropping 'floor vaults')."}
