{"type": "edge", "vol": "V10", "n": 1, "severity": "major", "items": ["V10-0493", "V09-0185", "V09-0559"], "where": "V10 §4.2 (3) creation acceptance and V09 §4.11 creation preview vs V09 §3.2 (3) the empty state", "claim": "V10 says that when a creation proposal replaces the untouched empty-state town 'the old handle closes — nothing is lost, the old town being its seed and still in the recent documents (R15)', and V09 §4.11 says 'the old one stays in Recent towns'; but V09 §3.2 (3) writes nothing to the local store while the log holds only its creation prefix (the LocalDocRecord is created on the first committed event), and the Recent grid (§5.13) lists stored towns. The edge 'accept an assistant's new town while the untouched empty-state town is open' has two outcomes in the set: the old town is recoverable from Recent, or it is gone.", "hint": "Rule the edge once: either the replaced empty-state town is written to Recent (a recipe-only record: seed and recipe, no snapshot) or it is dropped as V09 §3.2 drops it on Surprise me; make V09 §3.2, §4.11 and V10 §4.2 (3) say the same, with a bar."}
