{"type": "bref", "vol": "V09", "n": 3, "severity": "major", "items": ["V09-0001"], "where": "V09 passim (script: /private/tmp/claude-502/…/v09v10/bare-section-refs.json)", "claim": "The volume's convention says 'a section sign (§) points into the base', but lists continue a volume citation with bare signs ('V08 §5.1, §4.4, §3.1', 'V03 §4.5, §4.1', 'V11 §2.3–§2.4, §3.3.1'). A census of bare § references finds 165 that name no base section (e.g. §4.17, §4.20, §5.10, §2.12 — the volume's own) and 123 continuation references that do name an existing base section, so under the stated convention they resolve to the wrong target (e.g. 'V08 §5.1, §4.4' → base §4.4 Layers). Every cross-reference must resolve (principle (4)).", "hint": "Write the volume prefix on every section number (Vnn §x.y, one form), or state the list convention once in the canon and have the reference checker apply it; fix the 288 references."}
{"type": "bref", "vol": "V10", "n": 2, "severity": "major", "items": ["V10-0001"], "where": "V10 passim (script: bare-section-refs.json)", "claim": "Same class as V09: V10's convention says 'Section references without a prefix (§7.1, §11.2) are the base's', yet 211 bare § references name no base section (the volume's own §2.10, §3.16 …, or a sibling's) and 51 list continuations resolve to an existing but wrong base section (e.g. 'V09 §2.7, §2.9, §2.10, §3.9, §4.5' → base §2.9, §3.9, §4.5; 'V08 §3.1, §4.4, §5.4').", "hint": "Prefix every section number with its volume, or apply one canon list convention; fix the 262 references."}
{"type": "term", "vol": "V09", "n": 4, "severity": "minor", "items": ["V09-0199", "V09-0200", "V09-0287", "V09-0640"], "where": "V09 §3.7, §4.3, §4.5, §4.20.3, §5.x", "claim": "Several concepts carry more than one name inside the volume (principle (2)): the scoped regenerate is 'Try again' (the button), 'New random' (the base's action, mode newRandom), 're-roll' / 'scoped re-roll' and 'Rebuild … as generated' (history); a removal of generated content that holds is the 'suppression' (detail.suppress), 'the removal holds' (info.remove.holds), 'kept removed' (skeleton import) and 'Removals that hold' (file f item 260); the whole-town re-derivation is 'Re-derive' and 'Rebuild from {stage}'. UI words are catalogue data, but the design prose should use one concept name each.", "hint": "Canon glossary: one concept name each (e.g. 'scoped re-roll' = §7.1 New random; 'suppressing removal'; 'Re-derive'), UI words kept only as catalogue rows."}
